From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:44:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/40] cuda: hc_combine_norm writes the Q8_1 MMQ activation of
 its dense consumer (GGML_CUDA_HC_CN_MMQ_Q8=0: off)

In a qwen4exp prefill the fused hyper-connection combine + norm writes xn (F32, [n_embd*hc, T]), and the dense MUL_MAT
that reads it next (hc_down, a Q8_0 / D4-layout weight on MMQ) re-read all of it in quantize_mmq_q8_1 (~270 us per call
at T = 2048).  The combine kernel now also writes that MUL_MAT's block_q8_1_mmq activation in the same pass, with
quantize_mmq_q8_1<D4>'s expressions (a warp holds one 32-value scale group; amax, 127/amax, roundf, 1/d_inv), into a
single-slot handoff (mmq_q8_handoff, a pool-stack block reused while big enough and dropped at graph start / end like
bf16_src1_cache).  The consumer is found at fuse time and keyed by its node, src1 data, shape and stream; ggml_cuda_mul_mat_q
takes the block only on its plain dense path (no fusion, no swiglu, no FP4, D4 layout, unpadded contiguous src1) and
invalidates the key either way, so every other dispatch quantizes as before.  Scalar RMS mode only (the vec4 mode groups
8 lanes per scale group), multi-token (T >= 64), warp 32.  GGML_CUDA_HC_CN_MMQ_Q8=2 also runs the reference quantize and
compares the bytes on the host (debug; skipped inside a stream capture).

Prod config (2x R9700, -sm tensor): 31.5k prefill 3694 -> 3765 t/s (+1.9 %), 232k needle 3279 -> 3326 t/s (+1.4 %);
mode 2: 16,800 compares, 0 differ; prod-config references unchanged.
